    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d657">

                <pb facs="0918" n="812" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg812"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Jackson to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-01-23"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 23, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 360.—Greek Series.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Wilson’s dispatch No. 331,
                    this series, of October 20, 1905, and to your instruction No. 95, of November 8,
                    I <pb facs="0919" n="813" xml:id="pg813"/> have the honor to inclose herewith a
                    translation of a copy of the decision of the legal authorities—which I have just
                    received from the Greek minister of foreign affairs—upon the strength of which
                    Panos Indares was exempted from military service. This copy was sent me without
                    comment.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Jackson.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d657-a1.xml" xpointer="d657-a1"/>
            </div>
